12-Sep-2026  0.90.1 Fixes to make the 32-bit online build run under RISC OS 5
                    CPU alignment checking (ARMv7 default, e.g. Raspberry Pi 4).
                    The original binary used -memaccess -L22-S22-L41 (see 0.85)
                    to tolerate unaligned access; Norcroft cc 5.18 on the online
                    build service does not support that flag, so unaligned data
                    aborts ("type 20") had to be fixed in the source. Widened
                    three 16-bit globals the compiler read with unaligned word
                    loads: the MCS user id (mcs_connect), the server RDP version
                    (rdp_send_logon_info) and the sound sample width. Removed
                    -Otime. Restored abort/postmortem capture to
                    <Wimp$ScrapDir>.RDPClient.Error. Enlarged the 8-bit pixel
                    translation buffer to its true size (was a fixed 256 bytes).
                    24-bit display now connects with CPU alignment ON.
                    (8-bit colour still has outstanding issues -> 0.90.2.)
